<refnamediv>
  <refname><function>SilikoTokenGetId</function></refname>
  <refpurpose>Function to retrieve the identifier value of a
    token</refpurpose>
</refnamediv>

<refsynopsisdiv>
<programlisting language="C">#include &lt;SilikoCore/Token.h&gt;</programlisting>
<programlisting language="C">const char *SilikoTokenGetId(const SilikoToken *object);</programlisting>
</refsynopsisdiv>

<refsection>
<title>Description</title>
<para>The <function>SilikoTokenGetId</function> function gets the
identifier value of <varname>object</varname>.</para>
</refsection>

<refsection>
<title>Return Values</title>

<para><function>SilikoTokenGetId</function> returns the identifier
  value of <varname>object</varname> if <varname>object</varname>
  holds an identifier value. If <varname>object</varname> does not
  hold an identifier, then <function>SilikoTokenGetId</function> returns
  <literal>NULL</literal>. If <function>SilikoTokenGetId</function>
  returns a valid pointer, then the string pointed to is owned by
  <varname>object</varname> and must not be deallocated by the calling
  context.</para>
</refsection>
